# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession draft Alchemy --out` from Era-baseline data. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/alchemy
title Alchemy 1-300
category Professions
levels 5-60
zone Azeroth

# Era-baseline data:
# Blizzard Classic Era client tables (recipes, skill thresholds, reagents,
# vendor prices) via wago.tools, pfQuest (vendors, drops, nodes) and a curated
# trainer list checked against npcs.json. Nothing public confirms Forever
# changed profession recipes, so the Era recipe list is the baseline.
#
# Trainers and vendors are smart targets: the engine sends each character to
# the nearest one of its faction. Farming spots are picked per faction.
#
# Recipe choice: cheapest expected cost to 300 (Classic skill-up chances:
# certain while orange, falling from yellow to grey), with gathered materials
# valued at 4x their vendor sell price; see tools/lib/professions/plan.js.
# Material counts are expected values; yellow and green crafts can take more.
#
# Route:
#     1-75  Minor Healing Potion (about 82)
#    75-80  Minor Healing Potion (about 12)
#    80-100 Lesser Healing Potion (about 24)
#   100-150 Holy Protection Potion (about 58)
#   150-165 Fire Oil (about 27)
#   165-175 Elixir of Firepower (about 12)
#   175-225 Great Rage Potion (about 74)
#   225-245 Elixir of Greater Defense (about 43)
#   245-250 Elixir of Detect Undead (about 6)
#   250-259 Stonescale Oil (about 20)
#   259-265 Elixir of Detect Undead (about 11)
#   265-300 Elixir of Superior Defense (about 43)

step Apprentice Alchemy
  tip Alchemy runs alongside leveling. Forever's Legacy System rewards crafting professions at skill 150, 225 and 300 (the Journeyman, Expert and Artisan caps), so each of those checkpoints counts. Materials for 1-75 are worth about 68s in all.
  train Alchemy Apprentice
  skill Alchemy 1
  buy 3371 x82 nearest

